WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:06.730
This story is one that lightly describes the ordinary daily lives of the three Minami sisters.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.340
Please don't expect too much from it.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.300
Also, watch in a bright room,

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.990
and stay 3 meters away from the TV while watching.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:22.370
Kana

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:22.710
Chiaki

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:23.500
Haruka

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:50.040
Of Christmas and Eves

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:04.730
It's almost Christmas...

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:06.890
I wonder when that is coming...

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:11.560
When the topic of Christmas comes up, Chiaki gets a distant look in her eyes.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:15.280
Oh, Santa, huh?

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:17.530
That's what she'll say.

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:21.450
Didn't it all start two years ago?

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:26.160
Chiaki saw Takeru-ojisan putting on a beard in the changing room.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:33.460
Witnessing that must have been traumatic for her.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:36.590
I suppose that was when Chiaki lost her dreams.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:42.050
Takeru's the one who took her dreams!

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:44.260
Ojisan didn't mean anything bad.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.760
I'm sure he'll come again this year.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:50.390
Santa-san is going to ring the doorbell and enter through the front door.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.610
But I have to do something to bring her dreams back.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:57.100
That's right!

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.280
Can I have a minute, Haruka?

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:02.320
Christmas Eve

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.240
And now, for the news.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:09.460
The customary Loincloth Santa Festa has begun.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:11.560
Reporter, are you there?

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:13.670
Yes, I'm at the scene of the event.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:16.770
Don't you feel cold in this snow?

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:18.840
Ho Ho Ho!

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:22.570
Haruka-neesama, no Santa this year?

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:25.300
He's got something on.

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:30.270
You mean that Santa had no plans for Christmas until last year?

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:34.190
From what I saw a few days back, he doesn't look like he has plans this year either.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:38.440
<i>It's about time...</i>

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:43.680
Even though Kana-chan told me not to come,

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.990
I'm certain Chiaki-chan needs Santa.

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:48.450
Good evening!

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:50.630
Good evening...

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.190
You're on time!

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:01.800
Who's
he!?

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:04.890
Where do I change my clothes?

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:06.470
Be quiet.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:10.470
Oh, Haruka-chan?

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.890
Ojisan, you came?

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:18.070
No, that person is Kana's friend.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:19.980
Should I go sleep?

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:22.810
Tomorrow? Okay, I'll come tomorrow.

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:24.810
Alright!

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:29.240
Sorry for asking so much of you.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:32.460
Nope, it's my first time doing this, and it looks fun!

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:56.520
Merry Christmas!

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:05.660
Are you sure she saw you?

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:07.110
We made eye contact.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:09.030
Great! Well done!

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:14.530
Haruka-neesama!

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:17.250
Santa was in my room, and he wasn't Takeru!

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:18.620
Really?

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:19.810
That's nice.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:21.700
He left behind a present!

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:22.860
Really?

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.220
You're still awake?

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.640
Kana! Santa was here just now!

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:31.250
What do you mean, Santa?

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:33.250
Are you still a child?

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:34.640
What an idiot!

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:35.030
She has
always
wanted to
say that
What an idiot!

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:36.600
She has
always
wanted to
say that

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:38.060
He WAS here!

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:40.770
He was here!

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:44.330
Wipe that smirk off your face!

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:48.240
Why did it turn into a fight?

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:17.690
I feel so empty...

00:06:28.190 --> 00:06:30.970
There is someone I want you to meet.

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:50.260
What sweet dreams could she be having?

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:52.010
He WAS here!

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:54.060
The other Christmas

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:58.600
The Loincloth Santa Festival was well received when it started.

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:00.770
Christmas Eve is just around the corner.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:04.940
You shouldn't say "around the corner", isn't it today?

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:09.670
From now, Christmas Eve, until tomorrow, it will continue to snow...

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:13.620
Don't watch TV when we're discussing something important here.

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:15.620
Okay...

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:19.650
Concerning the Christmas present we're getting for Touma,

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:22.270
We've been holding meetings for one week,

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:23.540
And Christmas came before we knew it?

00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:26.500
Time doesn't wait for us.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:29.950
We have to come to a conclusion immediately and go buy it.

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:32.730
We already have a conclusion, don't we?

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:39.640
Touma has been saying lately that she wants a new soccer ball or new spiked shoes.

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:41.390
Come to think of it...

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:43.390
Right? That should do.

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:50.070
Akira, Natsuki, do you think that is what Touma truly wishes for?

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.380
What do you mean, bro?

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:59.540
It's true that Touma is a bit boyish when compared to girls of the same age.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:03.380
As expected, that's the result of growing up in the company of good-for-nothing brothers.

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:05.980
You can't be sure of that yet.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:10.880
What's that?

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:13.300
A letter to Santa Claus.

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:15.550
A letter to Santa?

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:18.250
Touma is at a difficult age.

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:20.980
Even though we are her family, there are things she can't tell us.

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:23.950
I don't think she holds back at all though.

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:29.960
If that comes in the form of a letter to Santa Claus...

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:32.030
I believe Touma will become more honest.

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:34.980
I can't believe Touma wrote that.

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:37.390
I suppose she still believes in Santa Claus.

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:38.820
Isn't she cute?

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:42.160
With this we can understand her true feelings.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:46.970
"Screw you, just hand over the new soccer ball or spike shoes", is what's written here.

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:50.380
Does this mean she can be honest with her feelings, even to Santa?

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:53.860
She addressed this letter to her brothers.

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:58.550
Now we know what Touma really wants.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:00.220
It's decided then?

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:05.020
That may be true, but those things don't feel feminine, do they?

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:07.310
I don't agree with you, bro.

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:11.210
We are in an age where it isn't weird for girls to be playing soccer.

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:12.650
Of course.

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:15.820
For instance, if my girlfriend likes soccer,

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:17.860
That's considered her charm point,

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:21.290
And I'll go all out to support her.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:25.220
Well, if you ask me what kind of girlfriend I choose...

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:27.260
Don't interrupt when adults are talking!

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:32.110
But I'm not talking about my imaginary girlfriend.

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:33.600
I'm talking about Touma.

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:35.170
So she doesn't exist?

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:37.320
Unfortunately.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:39.180
What about you?

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:40.490
I...

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:50.590
I may not look like it, but I'm always...

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:52.460
Stop interrupting!

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:56.450
What do we do?

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:59.070
What happened last Christmas?

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:02.410
I see. Our past experiences will be a good reference.

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:08.330
Touma was a crybaby back then.

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:13.970
However you think about it, the Christmas right after she was born can't be a good reference.

00:10:13.970 --> 00:10:14.880
In that case...

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:17.630
This was last year's Christmas.

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:20.510
Why was Touma looking so annoyed?

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:22.850
Let's go back in time a little.

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:25.520
She also looked annoyed the year before last.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:28.290
Is there a mystery hidden in all these?

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:30.150
Bro, let's continue.

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:31.230
Right.

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:34.190
This was Touma during her entrance ceremony for kindergarten.

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:36.900
That's her Coming of Age Ceremony, isn't it?

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:40.810
When she was that age, she'd follow us wherever we go.

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:46.190
Yeah. Because of her cuteness, she was popular among the neighbors.

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:56.140
It's Christmas, and you haven't prepared anything!

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:58.260
How long are you going to keep staring at the albums?!

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:03.180
Make it a proper Christmas once in a while, you stupid brothers!

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:08.940
I remember now...

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:13.080
In the end, we never could celebrate Christmas because of this.

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:17.770
As I thought, she became tomboyish because she's surrounded by us good-for-nothing brothers...

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:20.790
No, you can't be sure of that yet.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:42.180
The Christmas present I didn't have a chance to give Minami yesterday.

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:43.680
In the first place, for a so-called Christmas present...

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:46.890
The Minami's
In the first place, for a so-called Christmas present...

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:51.110
There should be no problem giving them on the day of Christmas itself.

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:55.810
But if Minami is the type of person who would get upset about that...

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:02.110
Fujioka, there's something I want you to taste!

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:06.780
Okay, I'm digging in!

00:12:08.590 --> 00:12:09.720
Does it taste good?

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:10.510
Yup!

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:14.660
Are you alright?

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:15.420
Yup.

00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:17.470
Are you telling the truth?

00:12:17.470 --> 00:12:18.870
Yeah...

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:23.780
Hey! It seems that it's okay even when it's three days past the "best before" date!

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:29.350
Well, the "best before" date and the expiry date are entirely different to begin with.

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:31.860
Even so you shouldn't eat it.

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:33.420
Okay!

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:38.790
Delicious!

00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:42.490
One day past should be okay, right?

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:48.370
Hello. Good evening.

00:12:48.820 --> 00:12:50.080
Good evening.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:51.320
Are they out?

00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:52.570
Seems so.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:01.540
Looks like it's going to snow again.

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:02.910
Yeah.

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:05.200
You came to deliver presents today?

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:08.190
Oh, I forgot this place yesterday...

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:10.320
Actually, me too.

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:11.520
Is that so?

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:25.420
Haruka-neesama.

00:13:25.420 --> 00:13:29.230
Is it really okay to be eating barbecue at a extravagant place like this?

00:13:29.230 --> 00:13:30.610
It's fine, it's fine!

00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:33.010
Let's splurge on Christmas Eve!

00:13:33.010 --> 00:13:34.270
My, my.

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:37.280
To be bounded by money matters at your age, how pathetic.

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:43.210
You have no idea how to enjoy life as a child.

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:46.680
Don't talk about enjoying life over a barbecue, you dumbass.

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:47.720
The same goes for you.

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:51.180
You should show more interest in the opposite sex, and not only your appetite, you dumbass.

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:56.260
In other words, don't get excited over a little food, you dumbass.

00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:58.150
Also I have one more thing to add.

00:13:58.150 --> 00:13:59.360
Dumbass.

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:02.200
A "dumbass" four-hit combo!

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:05.940
Even if you don't show it on your face, you are actually excited over this barbecue, aren't you?

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:07.950
I'm different from you.

00:14:08.730 --> 00:14:11.510
Customers at table number three, sorry for waiting!

00:14:13.150 --> 00:14:16.080
I feel like I've forgotten about something...

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:22.300
It's freezing.

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:23.800
Yeah.

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:28.560
I have to wake up early tomorrow too... I'm going back for today.

00:14:29.620 --> 00:14:31.570
Then I'll be going too.

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:34.410
Do you have work tomorrow?

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:36.940
Yeah. I have to go to Kyushu in the morning.

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:37.920
What about you?

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:40.480
I have club practice in the morning.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:42.730
Both of us have it tough.

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:44.490
Minami-ke!

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:48.350
Hey, Touma.

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:52.350
You are Chiaki's younger brother, right?

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:57.320
As long as the settings don't change, I'm a boy and a younger brother.

00:14:57.320 --> 00:15:00.640
When you return home, you go back to being a sister, don't you?

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:04.340
Otherwise my brothers would keep complaining.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:06.800
I can't sit cross-legged when I'm wearing a skirt.

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:12.970
But I can't believe you're leading a double life at your age.

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:16.320
Can those words be applied to her situation?

00:15:16.320 --> 00:15:21.650
Well, whether I'm a sister or a brother, you people decided without asking me.

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:25.410
While we're at it, perhaps I should try leading a double life.

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:29.560
You are really sudden.

00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:32.000
What will you do exactly?

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:33.820
Are you going to become a younger brother as well?

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:36.340
Let's see...

00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:39.930
I'll have breakfast at my house, lunch at school...

00:15:39.930 --> 00:15:43.550
Dinner at Touma's place, and afternoon snack at Keiko's place.

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:46.250
Also, I'll have supper at Uchida's place!

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:52.980
Rather than leading a double life, you're just being a thick-skinned glutton.

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:56.580
What's wrong?

00:15:56.580 --> 00:16:00.630
Umm, is it better for me to pay for the food expenses?

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:02.370
I eat here often anyway.

00:16:02.370 --> 00:16:04.720
Don't take that seriously.

00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:07.990
That's right! Pay up! 380 yen per meal per person!

00:16:07.990 --> 00:16:11.800
Don't give those numbers as if it's for real, dumbass!

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:12.960
I'm back!

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:19.400
Silly! You don't need to worry about that.

00:16:19.400 --> 00:16:23.790
If you are a younger brother to Chiaki, that means you're a younger brother to me too.

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:26.830
Haruka.

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:29.050
Haruma-neesama is right.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:33.240
Haruka, where's the afternoon snack?

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:36.720
You went to buy cake, right?

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:40.100
Oh my. Aren't you having your afternoon snack at Keiko's place?

00:16:46.140 --> 00:16:47.030
Does it taste good?

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:48.460
Tastes great!

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:49.440
It's delicious.

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:52.240
Really? That's great.

00:16:52.670 --> 00:16:56.390
Ah, Keiko? Cake would be nice for today's afternoon snack.

00:16:56.940 --> 00:16:58.950
What? You already had it?!

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:01.480
I'm going to leave fingerprints all over your glasses!

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:03.070
Damn you!

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:05.250
Minami-ke!

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:10.630
Welcome, welcome!

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:12.630
A limited time only year-end sale!

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:14.220
It's starting soon!

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:18.040
<i>I didn't manage to pass her the present during Christmas Eve or Christmas.</i>

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:22.040
<i>Today I'll definitely...</i>

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:25.270
Eggs! Eggs! Hmm... Eggs!

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:28.150
Minami! You came at the right time-
Eggs! Eggs! Hmm... Eggs!

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:32.820
First we're going with 1 yen for one box of eggs, limited to one per customer!

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:34.180
Go ahead!

00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:35.780
Lucky!

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:42.290
If I could pass this to her before the year ends...

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:47.750
The Loincloth Santa Festival held from yesterday night to this morning,

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:50.800
Ended without any casualties.

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:53.180
Welcome back, Kana.

00:17:53.180 --> 00:17:54.580
I'm back.

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:55.740
Hey, Haruka,

00:17:55.740 --> 00:17:58.520
The thing Chiaki is holding is Fujioka Santa's...

00:17:58.520 --> 00:18:01.050
Yup! Her Christmas present.

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:06.520
Looks like she likes the present.

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:12.190
But she's putting her elbow on its face.

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:15.380
In response to this entertaining event,

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:20.360
some questions were raised about whether wrapping presents with loincloths is unhygienic.

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:23.860
What kind of creature is that guy?

00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:25.860
Huh? A bear, of course.

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:27.460
A bear, huh...

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:29.630
It looks like it failed at catching fish...

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:38.050
This is the bear you got from Santa, right?

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:39.720
You should take good care of it.

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:41.190
<i>I am</i> taking good care of it.

00:18:41.190 --> 00:18:43.320
That was the bear's will.

00:18:43.320 --> 00:18:44.760
<i>Its will, eh?</i>

00:18:45.440 --> 00:18:48.380
<i>Even though she doesn't look interested in stuffed toys...</i>

00:18:49.360 --> 00:18:50.820
Does it have a name?

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:53.270
What childish things are you saying?

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:57.530
Don't hold it by its ear. It looks pitiful.

00:18:58.180 --> 00:19:00.040
I'm sorry.

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:04.180
Take care of it, okay? It's a bear from Santa, after all.

00:19:04.180 --> 00:19:06.070
That goes without saying.

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:08.910
In that case, we should give it a name, shouldn't we?

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:11.370
You give it a name then.

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:13.440
Eh? Me?

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:17.260
Fujioka?

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:26.200
It appears that it likes the name.

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:29.590
Then what was that attack just now?

00:19:29.590 --> 00:19:33.370
"I likes the name, I doesn't likes you."

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:35.230
That's what Fujioka said.

00:19:36.670 --> 00:19:39.440
What a cheeky stuffed toy we have here.

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:41.390
If I were in the same condition as when I was in Alaska,

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:45.020
I'd have hunted the likes of you along with the King Salmon."

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:46.410
That's what it's saying.

00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:49.870
Damn cheeky Fujioka!

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:52.860
I'll remove all of your cotton and torture you!

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:55.380
Come here!

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:57.830
"Don't pull me! It hurts!"

00:19:57.830 --> 00:19:59.090
Is what it's saying!

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:02.800
Shut up! I'll teach you about the harsh living conditions of Japan!

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:04.510
That's enough!

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:12.850
You just hit me with Fujioka, didn't you?

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:15.190
You have to take good care of it.

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:16.690
I am.

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:19.360
That was Fujioka's will.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:21.400
The next day...

00:20:23.510 --> 00:20:26.290
<i>Today I'll definitely pass this to Minami...</i>

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:28.850
Mi-Minami!

00:20:28.850 --> 00:20:30.620
Oh, Fujioka!

00:20:31.840 --> 00:20:36.350
You know, you have to consider the feelings of the person you're giving presents to.

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:40.620
Because of the present you gave Chiaki, I had a hard time.

00:20:40.620 --> 00:20:43.610
What's with that tough guy who came back from Alaska?

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:45.380
Huh? Alaska?

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:47.600
Okay then, I have shopping to do.

00:20:49.870 --> 00:20:52.980
<i>Consider the feelings of the person I'm giving presents to, huh?</i>

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:57.220
<i>If I give Minami this, will she be happy?</i>

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:04.990
I'm the only one who's happy about it all!

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:08.490
If I think about Minami's feelings in every way possible...

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:13.750
Kana? Fujioka-kun's here!

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:17.410
What? What a bother, and the weather's so cold.

00:21:23.220 --> 00:21:25.190
What's that?

00:21:25.190 --> 00:21:26.370
He gave me this.

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:29.490
What's this?

00:21:29.490 --> 00:21:31.490
Can't you tell by looking?

00:21:31.490 --> 00:21:34.910
It's boneless ham as thick as your thighs are.

00:21:34.910 --> 00:21:36.230
Okay. I'm going to punch you.

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:41.220
A year-end present?

00:21:41.220 --> 00:21:43.700
He doesn't have to go that far.

00:21:43.700 --> 00:21:45.320
Year-end present?

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:46.380
Ham...

00:21:49.100 --> 00:21:51.620
Is he like that Ham Guy in the commercials?!

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:55.750
<i>I... I gave it to her!</i>

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:59.220
<i>I gave it to her!</i>

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:31.210
Next Episode

00:23:31.210 --> 00:23:32.510
This year is coming to an end soon.
Next Episode

00:23:32.510 --> 00:23:33.190
This year is coming to an end soon.

00:23:33.190 --> 00:23:37.070
Let's make next year a good year too, Haruka-neesama.

00:23:37.070 --> 00:23:37.950
That's right.

00:23:37.950 --> 00:23:38.560
Next time, Love Going Around in Circles.

00:23:38.560 --> 00:23:40.150
Love Going
Around in Circles

00:23:40.150 --> 00:23:41.350
Huh? The two of us?

00:23:41.350 --> 00:23:44.540
Who else besides us?

00:23:44.540 --> 00:23:44.970
Love Going
Around in Circles
